{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1180872-designing-some-bloodlines","id":1180872,"title":"Designing some bloodlines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-30T13:45:00-08:00","id":1180872,"title":"Designing some bloodlines","content":"I'm creating some bloodlines, mainly VTM &quot;ports&quot;. What do you think?<br /> <br /> Followers of Set<br /> Parent clan: Mekhet<br /> Random infos: corruptors like their masquerade counterparts. They are not only a bloodline, but also a &quot;sect&quot; (idk if it's better to make them a covenant or a sub-group somewhere), and they teach Serpentis and their ways even if they are unable to join the actual bloodline (for any reason). <br /> Disciplines: celerity, obfuscate, auspex, serpentis (from the translation guide)<br /> Weakness: their blood potency is considered x2 higher when calculating sun damage, and bright light gives them the Disoriented condition<br /> Missing stuff: how could I make in the vtr metaplot the setite religion? Do you know any homebrew for the setite sorcery?<br /> <br /> Ravnos<br /> Parent clan: Nosferatu<br /> Random infos: they are almost the same as the vtm ones.<br /> Disciplines: resilience, animalism, nightmare, chimerstry<br /> Weakness: they have a vice (not a Vice), and must attempt a roll of some sort (ideas?) to avoid indulging in it<br /> Missing stuff: dice roll for the weakness, no idea for plot integration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My English sucks. Sorry.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23549-toreadorgentleman","name":"ToreadorGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T13:52:00-08:00","id":1180874,"title":"","content":"Good idea. You might check out the Vampire Translation Guide to help with others.<br /> <br /> It suggests either using the Followers of Set as a sect, rather than a clan, and giving them Theban Sorcery. Or having them as a Daeva bloodline. For the Ravnos it suggests making them their own clan, or if a bloodline, associating them with the Gangrel, 'but the Daeva better represent their outlook in the current World of Darkness.' Their weakness 'compels them to indulge in some form of trickery or deceit. Whenever the opportunity arises to do so, the player must roll Resolve + Composure -1 for every night in which the character has not indulged.' Though that might be updated a bit in second edition so that it's tied in with Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-30-2018, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T14:03:56-08:00","id":1180877,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the Mekhet Clanbook has presented the Followers of Set as a Shadow Cult, and gave them Cruac as their special shtick. Their ideology is pretty much the old Follower's faith, with all the emphasis upon chaos and such, even if with some differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}